 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios Workday shares have given back some of the gains from a Reuters report about a possible Silver Lake takeover, which would be one of the largest software buyouts ever.

 Workday was valued at around $43 billion before last Thursday's leak, after which shares surged around 18%. They've since retreated over 7%, for a $48.5 billion market cap. The S&amp;P Software Index, meanwhile, was down nearly 3% yesterday but remains up 18.5% for the year. 
 
